  h^0 \( C \, cal(O)_C \( Z \) \) = 1 \,\
h^0 \( C \, theta + H \) = 6 . $ <curve:section-dimensions>]

 More precisely,
#[#set math.equation(numbering: n => "(2.11)")
 $ H^0 \( C \, L \) & = xi H^0 \( C \, H \) \,\
H^0 \( C \, H + 2 Z \) & = xi^2 H^0 \( C \, H \) \,\
H^0 \( C \, theta \) & = xi^2 H^0 \( C \, 2 H \) . $ <curve:section-multiplication>]

 In particular $r = xi u$ is a basis of $H^0 \( C \, L \)$ with simple common zero divisor exactly $Z$,
