    volume. The differential $omega$ trivializes $K_Gamma$. For a line bundle $B$ on a smooth curve,
    the local pairing between principal parts of $B \( D \)$ and jets of $K - B$ is
  $ \( a \, s \) mapsto sum_(q in Z) "Res"_q \( a s \) . $
  It is perfect: in a parameter and mutually dual frames the two coefficients of $a_(- 2) z^(- 2) +
    a_(- 1) z^(- 1)$ pair with a jet $s_0 + s_1 z$ as $a_(- 2) s_1 + a_(- 1) s_0$.
    Consequently the two principal part spaces
  $ H^0 #h(-0.16667em) (C \, frac(cal(O)_C \( 3 H + 2 Z \), cal(O)_C \( 3 H \))) \, wide
    H^0 #h(-0.16667em) (Gamma \, frac(cal(O)_Gamma \( - N_Gamma + 2 Z \), cal(O)_Gamma \( - N_Gamma \))) $
  are both identified by residues with $H^0 \( D \, N_Sigma \|_D \)^(*)$.
    This defines their comparison without any choice of coordinates or frames.
    It compares the full local principal-part spaces before any condition of global realizability is imposed.
  Both complete adjoint systems are restrictions of the same ambient system $H^0 \( Sigma \, N_Sigma \)$.
    Indeed, the kernels in the restriction sequences to $C$ and to $Gamma$ are respectively
  $ cal(O)_Sigma \( - Gamma - 3 F \) = cal(O)_Sigma \( - 5 \, - 2 \) \, wide cal(O)_Sigma \( F \) =
    cal(O)_Sigma \( 1 \, 0 \) \, $
  and both have vanishing first cohomology. Their images on the common scheme $D$ therefore coincide.
    Equivalently, an ambient section vanishing on $Gamma$ vanishes to order at least four on $C$ at $Z$ and has no
    effect on these residue tests.
  The principal part exact sequence and Serre duality now say that the image of $H^0 \( C \, Lambda \)$,
    by $T mapsto "pp" \( T \/ xi^2 \)$, is precisely the annihilator of this common adjoint jet space;
    its kernel is $xi^2 H^0 \( C \, 3 H \)$. On $Gamma$ the same annihilator is the image of
  $ H^0 \( Gamma \, Phi \) arrow.r
    H^0 #h(-0.16667em) (Gamma \, frac(cal(O)_Gamma \( - N_Gamma + 2 Z \), cal(O)_Gamma \( - N_Gamma \))) \, wide
    tilde(T) mapsto "pp" \( tilde(T) \/ beta^2 \) \, $
  because $Phi = 2 M - N_Gamma$ and $\( beta \) = Z$. This map is injective:
    its kernel would give a section of $- N_Gamma$, which has degree $- 10$. These facts establish (3.4).
