    For an ambient test section $A \( y \, z \) frak(g) frak(f)$, the two residue tests are
  #[#set math.equation(numbering: n => "(3.8)")
   $ "Res"_0 #h(-0.16667em) (frac(A \|_C thin pi thin e \|_C, k_y \|_C thin z^2) thin d z) \, wide
     "Res"_0 #h(-0.16667em) (frac(A \( 0 \, z \) thin tilde(pi), b \( z \)^2) thin d z) . $ <trace:local-residue-tests>]
  The restrictions of $A$ to the two curves agree modulo $z^4$.
    It follows from (3.5) that equality of their residue functionals on all local test jets is exactly
  #[#set math.equation(numbering: n => "(3.9)")
   $ "pp" #h(-0.16667em) (frac(pi, K \( z \) z^2)) = "pp" #h(-0.16667em) (frac(tilde(pi), b \( z \)^2)) \, wide
